    "reason": "[ev-cb880878ba69] says only that `istio.io/gateway-name` was removed and that the `gateway.networking.k8s.io/gateway-name` label should be used instead. It doesn't say whether this is a label Istio reads from user resources, which would no longer be honoured (setting-ignored), or a label Istio puts on the gateway resources it generates, so that selectors relying on it would stop matching. It also doesn't say what fails if nothing is done. The rest of the traffic-management section adds nothing on this. We need upgrade-guide text or the linked PR/code showing where the label is used and what breaks before a mandatory-work kind can be confirmed.",
